<===> README.md
Like dart-sass, `color.adjust()`, `color.change()` and `color.scale()` only
accept one positional argument, also if keyword arguments are passed too
(libsass silently ignored the extra positional arguments then).
<===>
================================================================================
<===> adjust/input.scss
@use "sass:color";
a {b: color.adjust(red, 10, $lightness: 5%)}
<===> adjust/error
Error: Only one positional argument is allowed. All other arguments must be passed by name.
  ,
2 | a {b: color.adjust(red, 10, $lightness: 5%)}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> change/input.scss
@use "sass:color";
a {b: color.change(red, 10, $red: 1)}
<===> change/error
Error: Only one positional argument is allowed. All other arguments must be passed by name.
  ,
2 | a {b: color.change(red, 10, $red: 1)}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> scale/input.scss
@use "sass:color";
a {b: color.scale(red, 10, $lightness: 5%)}
<===> scale/error
Error: Only one positional argument is allowed. All other arguments must be passed by name.
  ,
2 | a {b: color.scale(red, 10, $lightness: 5%)}
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 2:7  root stylesheet
